# text = My father looked carelessly at the title page of my book and said If , instead of this remark , my father had taken the pains to explain to me that the principles of Agrippa had been entirely exploded and that a modern system of science had been introduced which possessed much greater powers than the ancient , because the powers of the latter were chimerical , while those of the former were real and practical , under such circumstances I should certainly have thrown Agrippa aside and have contented my imagination , warmed as it was , by returning with greater ardour to my former studies .
